    "id" : 54,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 62.667, 346.89, 532.667, 385.557 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Although various PINN models have been successfully applied to the study of ordinary and partial differential equations, particularly in the case of the wave equation, our investigation shows that their performance deteriorates in large scale domain and long time range, potentially leading to non-convergence. For example, let us consider two scenarios for two-dimensional wave propagation equation with Dirichlet"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 55,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 62.333, 311.89, 532.0, 349.223 ],
    "font" : null,
    "font size" : 12.0,
    "content" : "For example; let us consider two scenarios for two-dimensional wave propagation equation with Dirichlet = The governed equation is"
  }, {
    "type" : "formula",
    "pdfua_tag" : "Formula",
    "id" : 56,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 231.667, 280.89, 532.667, 304.89 ],
